    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Issue #24019 reports rolling cov/corr on Series([1e5,0,0,0,0]) and Series([9.45]*5) where rolling(5).cov(b).iloc[4] differs from a.cov(b), and rolling corr yields inf instead of nan.",
      "The reproduction asserts exact equality (assert c1 == c2 and assert v1 == v2), not an explicit numeric tolerance; no tolerance value is stated in the passages.",
      "The regression test test_rolling_cov_corr_degenerate expects corr to be [nan]*5 and cov to be [nan,nan,nan,nan,0.0] for this input, compared with tm.assert_series_equal.",
      "The aggregations.pyx diff uses add_cov/remove_cov with a numerically_unstable flag that triggers a full recompute, and calc_corr returns NaN when ssqdm_x or ssqdm_y is 0.0, clamping val to [-1,1].",
